# KOL Task Enforcement (Cursor)

Applies to any KOL discovery, creator search, or influencer tracking task.

## Before any browse or Notion write

1. Read `.claude/skills/kol-discovery/SKILL.md`
2. Read `context/kol-brief-templates.md` — walk brand owner through template if brief incomplete
3. Read `context/brand-context.md` → **KOL Discovery Gates**
4. Read `.claude/skills/update-notion/SKILL.md` before Notion writes
5. Load platform skills per brief: `platform-instagram`, `platform-youtube`, `platform-youtube-shorts` as needed
6. Run `node tools/sync-kol-list.js` — read `context/kol-exclusion-list.md`
7. **Chrome health check** — call Chrome MCP `list_pages`. If disconnected: **stop all Instagram work** (hard stop). YouTube API work may continue if brief allows.

## Instagram rate-limit prevention (hard rules — enforce every session)

**Max 10 Chrome profile navigations per hour.** Count every `navigate_page` call to any `instagram.com` URL. Stop and pause 5+ minutes when approaching the limit.

**Pre-screen before Chrome.** For every candidate handle:
1. `node tools/sync-kol-list.js --check @handle` — dedup first
2. Web search via Socialpruf / Viralist / Google — confirm follower count, ER estimate, country signal
3. Only open Chrome for handles that passed both steps above

**Never browse blind.** Do not loop through tagged posts, following lists, or search results by navigating to each profile. Extract handles via `take_snapshot` + grep first, pre-screen externally, then open only the passing ones in Chrome.

**On first suspension signal** (`accounts/suspended` in URL): stop all Chrome IG work immediately. Do not retry. Switch to web search. Resume Chrome after 30+ minutes.

**Wait 4–5 seconds between navigations.** Use `AwaitShell block_until_ms: 4500` after each navigate call.

